          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A realizability topos is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            which embodies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+interpretation"} realizability interpretation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+mathematics"} intuitionistic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            (due to Kleene) as part of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+toposes"} elementary toposes
            that are not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            The input datum for forming a realizability topos is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+combinatory+algebra"} partial combinatory algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                When the PCA is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleene%27s+first+algebra"} Kleene's first algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒦
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+topos"} effective topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi RT
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒦
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RT(\mathcal{K}_1)
            %li
              %p
                When the PCA is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleene%27s+second+algebra"} Kleene's second algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒦
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_2
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi RT
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒦
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RT(\mathcal{K}_2)
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+realizability+topos"} function realizability topos
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %p
            There are a number of approaches toward constructing realizability toposes. One is through
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tripos"} tripos
            theory, and another is through assemblies (actually the latter is a family of related approaches).
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+combinatory+algebra"} PCA
            — in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#via_tripos_theory Via tripos theory
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tripos"} tripos
            whose base category is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            and for which the preorder
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_A(X)
            of
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A)^X
            of functions from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powerset"} powerset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \le \psi
            if there exists
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in \phi(x)
            implies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\cdot b \in \psi(x)
            for all
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            must be chosen uniformly across all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
          %p
            Applying the tripos-to-topos construction to this tripos produces the realizability topos over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tripos"} tripos
            for details.
          %h3#via_assemblies Via assemblies
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Asm
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Asm_A
            be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/assemblies"} assemblies
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+combinatory+algebra"} partial combinatory algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PAsm
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PAsm_A
            be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partitioned+assemblies"} partitioned assemblies
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong realizability topos
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ex%2Freg+completion"} ex/reg completion
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Asm
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Asm_A
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              In the presence of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ex%2Flex+completion"} ex/lex completion
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PAsm
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PAsm_A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Asm
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Asm_A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reg%2Flex+completion"} reg/lex completion
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PAsm
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PAsm_A
          #pax.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              A general result about the ex/lex completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
              of a left exact category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is that it has enough regular
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projectives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(P, -) \colon C_{ex/lex} \to Set
              preserves regular epis. In fact, the regular projective objects coincide with the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (as a subcategory of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
              is a topos, where every epi is regular, this means
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
              has enough projectives, or satisfies (external)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/internally+projective+object#enough"} this result
          #ac.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The fact that a realizability topos is an ex/lex completion depends on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
              holds in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Asm
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Asm_A
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#Characterization Axiomatic characterization
          %p
            The following is a statement characterizing realizability toposes which is analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giraud+axioms"} Giraud axioms
            characterizing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to) a realizability topos precisely if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
